    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d534">

                <pb facs="0516" n="508" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg508"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115/879: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-03-11T18:00:00-05:00">March 11, 1940—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>87. Reference Canton’s telegrams of February 9, 6 p.m., and March 5, 3
                        p.m.,<anchor n="69" xml:id="d534-f1"/> in regard to oil monopoly in Namhoi
                    district. The Department authorizes you in your discretion to make appropriate
                    representations to the Japanese Foreign Office.<anchor n="70" xml:id="d534-f2"
                    /></p>
                <p>Sent to Tokyo via Peiping. Repeated to Canton and Chungking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d534-f1" n="69" xml:id="d534-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d534-f2" n="70" xml:id="d534-f2-content">
                <p>See note No. 1498, March 20, from the American Ambassador in Japan to the
                    Japanese Minister for Foreign Affairs, <ref target="frus1931-41v01#pg_860"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 860</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
